node_modules/
dist/
target/
.DS_Store

# Release assembly output (scripts/build-release.ps1 regenerates it clean) — local build artifacts, never commit (ADR-0100).
release/

# launch/ = the local release build+run folder. The launchers (build/run .bat) are committed; only the build output is ignored.
launch/release/

# Local runtime data (daemon token · profiles etc.) — never commit. The default data_dir location of debug builds (ADR-0264).
/.engram-dev/
# The dev data folder under its old name — the code no longer reads or deletes it, but it stays listed so a leftover folder does not show up as untracked.
.engram-data/

# Runtime data of the release distribution (`data/` next to the executable — ADR-0134). Never commit it, for the same reason:
#   daemon\run\ holds the 256-bit WS token (daemon.json) and the tokens of the spawn attachment files (mcp-config\),
#   and daemon\state\agent-profiles.json holds the profiles (may include plaintext env) (old version = daemon\state\agents.json).
#
# ★Do not block it with a single folder-name line (`data/`) (do not bring it back)★: since the ADR-0134 rename the name is common, so it would
#   quietly swallow unrelated data folders too — ignoring is invisible, so a broad rule is worse than none.
# ★But do not delete these either★: the assembly output paths (release/ · launch/release/ · target/ above) are already covered, but
#   unzipping the distribution zip at **an arbitrary place** inside a tracked folder or running build-release.ps1 elsewhere with -OutDir
#   lands outside those paths. This part aims precisely at the secret locations only.
# ★Do not drop the trailing `*` of `agent-profiles.json*` · `agents.json*`★: the `.corrupt` · `.corrupt-*` copies and the atomic-write
#   temp files (`.tmp<pid>.<n>`) carry the same plaintext env.
# ★Do not delete the old-version `agents.json*` line either★: the new version neither reads nor deletes that file (ADR-0314 decision 5), so it stays in the folder.
# ★`daemon/run/` is a folder rule★ (ADR-0264 decision 7 — the only exception to the file-name principle of ADR-0136 decision 3)
#   — everything that holds a token (daemon.json · mcp-config\) is under it, and the path is specific, so it does not swallow
#   unrelated folders.
**/data/daemon/run/
**/data/daemon/state/agent-profiles.json*
**/data/daemon/state/agents.json*
# Secret files of the old flat layout — the code no longer reads or deletes them (ADR-0264 decision 5), but they stay listed so leftover tokens · plaintext env
#   do not show up as untracked and get committed by mistake.
**/data/daemon.json
**/data/agents.json*

# Handoff history (for /engram-handoff) — tracked in git to preserve the record (2026-07-09, user decision). history/ is append-only.
.ccb/

# Working screenshot store (cdp shot etc.) — local only, not committed.
_wip/shots/

# dev/daemon debug logs — local runtime output, never commit.
*.log

# Temporary test/debugging output (local only).
.resume-test-aid.txt
/tree-nested*.png
# Debug screenshots leaking to the root (cdp shot etc. are routed to _wip/shots/) — prevents a recurrence.
/*.png

# Visual Studio IDE scratch (solution cache · window state) — local only, never commit.
.vs/

# Measurement · review scratch (roundtrip phase runs · codex review output) — disposable; can be cleaned up after consulting it when re-measuring.
.codex/
